#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/folio-review-publish.bpmn:18
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Review a rendered folio and publish it, or send it back with changes. Shared by every authoring process: authoring-a-document (this layer) and authoring-a-paper (folio-assistant-sci) call it after they validate and render, so review, publish and committee feedback are drawn once. What differs by folio kind stays with the caller: its writing loop, its own check (the content profile for a document, the Lean build for a paper), and its renderer. It ends one of three ways. `Published`: the caller closes its bean. `Changes asked` and `Feedback in: changes asked`: the caller goes back to its writing loop."
msgstr ""

