#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/folio-review-publish.bpmn:66
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "See draft-to-publication.bpmn for the review and release path this expands into. Release authorisation is not relaxable."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/folio-review-publish.bpmn:42
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The calling authoring process has validated and rendered the folio. What the reviewer reads is the rendered artefact, never a description of it."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/folio-review-publish.bpmn:85
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The committee's feedback is in. Like `Changes asked`, the caller goes back to writing, so the feedback passes the same checks as any other edit."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/folio-review-publish.bpmn:36
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The people writing the document with the editor. While it is a working draft they give feedback through the Contributor Feedback sheet, one change set per row, and each row runs Process_ContributorFeedback."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/folio-review-publish.bpmn:46
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The reviewer this folio binds. authoring-document relaxes the base SME step precisely because no single lane fits every document. Review the rendered folio, not a description of it, and record the feedback. The outcome is iterate — back to authoring — or approved for the publication path."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/folio-review-publish.bpmn:55
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The reviewer's call after the review. `approved` goes to publish. `iterate` ends this process with changes asked, and the caller returns to its own writing loop with the feedback. `Authoring Committee feedback` sends a working draft to the committee through the Contributor Feedback sheet; what comes back is also changes asked."
msgstr ""
